{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a count of Tripoli who ruled from 1171 to 1193. He was a significant figure in the Crusader states and a military leader known for his successes against the Ayyubid Sultanate. His reign marked a period of stability and expansion for the Countship of Tripoli.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond III was the son of Raymond IV Count of Tripoli. He inherited the title upon his father's death in 1171. His early reign was characterized by consolidating power within the Countship and dealing with internal factions. He navigated the complex political landscape of the Crusader states skillfully. Raymond III’s ascension was not without challenges as he needed to solidify his position against rivals for control of the region. He demonstrated political acumen early on establishing alliances and managing the affairs of the Countship.\n\nRaymond III’s rule was marked by military campaigns and diplomatic efforts. He faced numerous threats from the Ayyubid Sultanate particularly under Saladin. He actively engaged in military conflicts defending Tripoli's territory and securing its borders. Raymond III was a capable military strategist and his campaigns often resulted in victories demonstrating his leadership abilities.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts*\n\nRaymond III’s military campaigns were a defining aspect of his reign. He engaged in several significant battles against the Ayyubids. These conflicts often involved sieges and skirmishes along the frontier. Raymond III successfully defended Tripoli from numerous Ayyubid incursions. His military successes significantly bolstered the prestige and power of the Countship.\n\nOne of the most notable campaigns was against Saladin's forces during the Third Crusade. Although Raymond III did not directly participate in the main Crusader armies he played a crucial role in defending Tripoli from Ayyubid attacks during the siege of Acre. His efforts helped to prevent the capture of Tripoli and preserved the Countship’s autonomy. The battles he fought showcased his tactical skills and his commitment to defending the Crusader territories.\n\n*Legacy and Death*\n\nRaymond III’s reign was a period of relative peace and prosperity for the Countship of Tripoli. He expanded the territory of the Countship and strengthened its defenses. His leadership helped to maintain a degree of autonomy for Tripoli within the Crusader states.\n\nRaymond III died in 1193 at the age of 51. His death marked the end of a period of stability and the beginning of a new era in the history of Tripoli. His legacy as a successful military leader and a capable ruler was widely respected throughout the Crusader territories. He is remembered as one of the most effective counts of Tripoli and a key figure in the defense of the Crusader states against the Ayyubids. His contributions to the defense of Tripoli and his successful governance left a lasting impact on the region.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1804991215467453}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.115249561844394e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.08474750816822052}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.03216259181499481}, {"token": "▁count", "logprob": -2.6424951553344727}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -0.07219361513853073}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -0.008959922008216381}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.19882245361804962}, {"token": "▁ruled", "logprob": -0.28537675738334656}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -0.003928089048713446}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0032151455525308847}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0002146728802472353}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0020063049159944057}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -2.765892267227173}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.